{
  "doc_id": "MIMIC_IV_NOTE:18669279-DS-17:discharge_sections",
  "register": "notes",
  "source_dataset": "MIMIC_IV_NOTE",
  "text": "Allergies:\nNo Known Allergies / Adverse Drug Reactions\n\nChief Complaint:\nfatigue, malaise, cough\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nPt is a ___ Y F with Stage Ia carcinosarcoma of the uterus; \npT1a,N0(0 of 29 pelvic, 0 of 24 paraaortic) Mx on ___ \n(last dose ___ who presents to the ER with fatigue and fever.  \nShe has been receiving Neulasta for chemo-associated \nneutropenia, last dose ___.  For 2 days prior to admission, \nshe complained of having generalized fatigue, malaise, and \nrinorrhea with clear secretions without headache, sinus \npressure, itchy eyes, or sore throat.  The day of admission, she \nhad a mild cough which was non-productive.  She took her \ntemperature which was 100.6.  She states that her husband has \nhad a URI viral syndrome for about a month but she has had no \nother sick contacts.  She does not have any urinary symptoms, \nabdominal pain, headache or meningeal signs.  She went to the ER \nwhere her initial bp was 98/62 with HR 76.  She received a total \nof 2L IVF and bp improved to 134/74; she denied lightheadedness \nor dizziness before.  She also received Vancomycin 1g IV, \nCefepime2g, and Tylenol ___ PO.  On arrival to the floor, she \nstates that she feels about at baseline for where she has been \nfor the past 2 days. \n\nReview of Systems:  \n(+) Per HPI, constipation\n(-) Denies chills, night sweats, recent weight loss or gain. \nDenies blurry vision, diplopia, loss of vision, photophobia. \nDenies headache, sinus tenderness. Denies chest pain or \ntightness, palpitations, lower extremity edema. Denies DOE, \nshortness of breath, or wheezes. Denies nausea, vomiting, \ndiarrhea, abdominal pain, melena, hematemesis, hematochezia. \nDenies dysuria, stool or urine incontinence. Denies arthralgias \nor myalgias. Denies rashes or skin breakdown. No \nnumbness/tingling in extremities. All other systems negative.\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\nPt is a ___ Y F with Stage Ia carcinosarcoma of the uterus; \npT1a,N0(0 of 29 pelvic, 0 of 24 paraaortic) Mx on ___ \n(last dose ___ who presents to the ER with fever.\n#Fever/? early Pneumonia - Pt admitted non-neutropenic fever( \nhas not reached nadir yet).CXR showed a possible new opacity \nwhich could be pneumonia vs atelectasis.However,pt w/o a cough \n/cp/or sob. Pt was started empirically on levofloxacin to cover \na  possible CAP in a pt high risk to develop neutropenia.Blood \nand urine cultures remained sterile.\n  \n#Stage Ia carcinosarcoma of the uterus on adjuvant ___. \nPt will continue f/u with .her primary oncologist  \n#Leukocytosis -Likely from from Neulasta.  \n#Mild Hypotension(BP in the ED 98/62) with lactacemia- Resolved \nafter IVF in ER.\n#Constipation - new without complicating features, colace, \nsenna, mirilax  \n#Hypothyroidism - chronic, stable; cont Synthroid  \n#Chronic pain - chronic, stable, continue fentanyl    \n#PPx - ambulatory  \n#FULL CODE\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nFever\nUpper respiratory infection/Community acquired pnumonia\nUterine cancer\nHypokalemia",
